Task 1: Install Required Packages
Subtask 1.1: Install nfs-utils and cifs-utils
These packages provide the tools needed to work with NFS and CIFS shares.

# Update package repositories
sudo dnf update -y

# Install NFS and CIFS utilities
sudo dnf install -y nfs-utils cifs-utils
Verification:

# Verify installations
rpm -q nfs-utils cifs-utils
Expected Output:

nfs-utils-2.x.x
cifs-utils-6.x.x
Troubleshooting Tip:

If using Ubuntu/Debian, replace dnf with apt and package names may vary slightly.
Task 2: Mount NFS Shares
Subtask 2.1: Discover Available NFS Shares
First, check what shares are available from the NFS server.

# Discover NFS shares (replace SERVER_IP with actual NFS server IP)
showmount -e SERVER_IP
Expected Output:

Export list for SERVER_IP:
/share  *
Subtask 2.2: Create a Mount Point and Mount NFS Share
# Create a local directory for mounting
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/nfs_share

# Mount the NFS share (replace SERVER_IP and /share with actual values)
sudo mount -t nfs SERVER_IP:/share /mnt/nfs_share
Verification:

# Check mounted filesystems
df -hT | grep nfs

# List contents of the mounted share
ls /mnt/nfs_share
Troubleshooting Tip:

If mount fails, ensure NFS services are running on the server: systemctl status nfs-server.
Task 3: Mount CIFS/SMB Shares
Subtask 3.1: Create Credentials File (Optional but Recommended)
Store CIFS credentials securely.

# Create a credentials file (replace USERNAME and PASSWORD)
echo "username=USERNAME" | sudo tee /etc/cifs_credentials > /dev/null
echo "password=PASSWORD" | sudo tee -a /etc/cifs_credentials > /dev/null

# Set restrictive permissions
sudo chmod 600 /etc/cifs_credentials
Subtask 3.2: Mount CIFS Share
# Create mount point
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/cifs_share

# Mount CIFS share (replace SERVER_IP and SHARENAME)
sudo mount -t cifs -o credentials=/etc/cifs_credentials //SERVER_IP/SHARENAME /mnt/cifs_share
Verification:

# Check mounted filesystems
df -hT | grep cifs

# List contents
ls /mnt/cifs_share
Troubleshooting Tip:

If mount fails, install samba-client for additional tools: sudo dnf install samba-client.
Task 4: Configure Persistent Mounts in /etc/fstab
Subtask 4.1: Add NFS Share to /etc/fstab
# Backup fstab
sudo cp /etc/fstab /etc/fstab.bak

# Add NFS entry (replace SERVER_IP and /share)
echo "SERVER_IP:/share  /mnt/nfs_share  nfs  defaults  0 0" | sudo tee -a /etc/fstab
Subtask 4.2: Add CIFS Share to /etc/fstab
# Add CIFS entry (replace SERVER_IP and SHARENAME)
echo "//SERVER_IP/SHARENAME  /mnt/cifs_share  cifs  credentials=/etc/cifs_credentials,uid=1000,gid=1000  0 0" | sudo tee -a /etc/fstab
Verification:

# Test fstab entries (mount all)
sudo mount -a

# Verify mounts persist after reboot (optional: reboot to test)
df -hT | grep -E 'nfs|cifs'
Troubleshooting Tip:

If mounts fail at boot, add _netdev option to fstab for network filesystems.
